# Calamus 1.09N (DMC, German), high resolution, 4 MB: an empty new
# document printed with the only driver on its disk, an HP LaserJet Plus
# (DRUCKER\HP_LJETP.CPD): the question is whether Calamus prints through TOS or
# drives the port itself (Atarimania's iPRN page: Calamus 1.x does the
# latter). Drive A is a work copy of its disk: DESKTOP.INF/NEWDESK.INF
# autostart A:\CALAMUS.PRG, and CALAMUS.SET's folders, E:\CALAMUS1.09N\ and
# E:\CALAMUS_.SL\ on the uploader's hard disk, point at A:\ with
# HP_LJETP.CPD as the printer (disk_copy.py --put). Positions are high
# resolution's (640 x 400).
@printer
@monitor mono
@memsize 4
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/calamus.st
wait 7000
# the first click after boot is lost: an empty spot first
mouse 500 300
click left 2
wait 25
# Datei > Neu anlegen
mouse 73 8
wait 25
mouse 105 27
click left 2
wait 200
shot new
# no fonts on the disk: Abbruch
mouse 315 252
click left 2
wait 100
# Datei > Drucken (einstellen)
mouse 73 8
wait 25
mouse 155 171
click left 2
wait 200
shot printdlg
# DRUCKEN with the defaults (150 x 150 dpi, A4, Parallel)
printwatch
mouse 126 366
click left 2
printer 1000 60000
shot printed
